\section{Step 1: Calculate the volume of the entire prism $ABCDEF$.}
The formula to calculate the volume of a prism is base area $\times$ height. The base area of this prism is the area of an equilateral triangle with side length 12. Since the height of the prism is 16, the volume of $ABCDEF$ can be calculated as:

\begin{align*}
\mbox{Volume}&=\mbox{base area}\times\mbox{height}\\
&=(\frac{1}{2}\times\mbox{sine of the base angle}\times\mbox{side length}^2)^2\times\mbox{height}\\
&=(\frac{1}{2}\times\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\times 12^2)^2\times 16\\
&=864\mbox{ cubic units}
\end{align*}
