The problem is \begin{align*} 
\text{Solve:} \qquad 50 + m + m + h - 100 &amp;= 80 \\
\text{This is the same:}\qquad m + m + h &amp;= 80 - 50 + 100 \\ 
\text{Subtract 100 off the left:}\qquad m +  m + h &amp;= 130   \\ 
\text{Factor out the one m-like term:}\qquad 2 m + h &amp;= 130. 
\end{align*} 
Since $n = h$, then  what is $n$, given $2m=n $?






\begin{align*}
2m+n&amp;=130\\
2n+n&amp;=130\\
3n&amp;=130\\
\frac{3n}{3}&amp;=\frac{130}{3}\\
n&amp;=\boxed{\frac{130}{3}}\text{ units} 
\end{align*}

\end{document}

``` -ShellFixProg```python
import sympy as sp

def solve_problem():
    n = sp.symbols('n')
    m = 2*n
    eq = 2*m + n -130
    sol = sp.solve(eq, n)
    return sol[0]

n = solve_problem()
print(f"The final answer is $\boxed{{{n}}}$")
```

The final answer is \boxed{\frac{130}{3}} cubic centimeters. 
Possible issue for human solvers is if they remember they used n = h.
