## Step 1: Recall the formula for the magnitude of a vector
The magnitude or norm of a vector $\mathbf{u}$, denoted $\| \mathbf{u} \|,$ can be computed as \[ \| \mathbf{u} \| = \sqrt{u_1^2 + u_2^2 + \ldots + u_n^2}. \]

## Step 2: Recall the formula for the dot product of two vectors
The dot product of two vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$, denoted $\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}$, can be computed as \[ \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = a_1b_1 + a_2b_2 + \ldots + a_nb_n. \]

## Step 3: Recall the formula for the magnitude of the sum of two vectors
\begin{align*}
\| \mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w} \|^2 &= (\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}) \cdot (\mathbf{v} + \mathbf{w}) \\
&= \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{v} + 2 \mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} + \mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}.
\end{align*}

## Step 4: Apply the formula to the problem at hand
Here, we need to compute the magnitude of the sum of $2 \mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$. Since $\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} = \left\|\mathbf{a}\right\|^2 = 3^2 = 9$ and $\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \left\|\mathbf{b}\right\|^2 = 8^2 = 64$, we can rewrite the expression as \begin{align*} \|2 \mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b}\|^2 = \left\|2 \mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} \right\|^2 = (2 \mathbf{a}) \cdot (2 \mathbf{a}) + 2(2 \mathbf{a}) \cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}. \end{align*}

## Step 5: Calculate each term
Using the properties of the dot product, we have \begin{align*}
    & \ (2 \mathbf{a}) \cdot (2 \mathbf{a}) = 4 \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{a} = 4 \cdot 9 = 36\\
    &  \ 2 ( 2 \mathbf{a})\cdot \mathbf{b}= 4 \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}\\
    & \  \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b} = 64.
\end{align*}

## Step 6: Use the formula for the dot product of two vectors.
\begin{align*}
    & \ \quad \mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \left\| \mathbf{a} \right\| \left\| \mathbf{b} \right\| \cos{\theta} = (3) (8)\cos{135^\circ} = -24
\end{align*}

## Step 7: Combine the terms
Now we can combine all the terms together to get:
\begin{align*}
    \left\| 2\mathbf{a} + \mathbf{b} \right\|^2 &= \left\| 2 \mathbf{a } \right\| \left\|\mathbf{b} \right\|^2 + 2 ( 2 \mathbf{a})\cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}\\
    &= ( 2)^2 \left\|\mathbf{a} \right\|^2 + 4 \mathbf{a}\cdot \mathbf{b} + \mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}\\
    &= 36 +  4 ( -24 ) + 64\\
    & = \boxed{64}
 \text{ square units}.
