If your unit and the result are integers, write the \text{ unit } as "units".


I begin by working from the inside of the problem, starting with the expression \left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2.  
\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2 = \frac{3^2}{4^2} = \frac{3^2}{\left(2^2\right)^2} = \frac{3^2}{\left(2^4\right)}  = \frac{9}{16}.
The rest of the problem is
\frac{20 \cdot \frac{2^2}{5 ^2} \cdot \left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2 \cdot \frac{5}{9}}{\text{ units }}
I evaluate it from left to right.
\begin{align*}
&{\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)^2 = \frac{9}{16}\\
& \ldftnoeq(20 \cdot \frac{2^2}{5^2} \cdot \frac{9}{16} \cdot \frac{5}{9} \right)^5}
\end{align*}
    \begin{align*}
& 20 \cdot \frac{\left(2^2\right)}{\left(5^2\right)} \cdot \frac{9}{16} \cdot \frac{5}{9}\\\\
&\,=  20 \cdot \frac{\left(4\right)}{\left(25\right)} \cdot \frac{1}{\left(16\right)} \cdot 1\\\\
&\,=20 \cdot \frac{\left(4\right)}{\left(25\right) \cdot \left(16\right)\\
&\,=\frac{80}{\left(400\right)
\end{align*}
Now, raise it to the 5th power
\begin{align*}
&\frac{80}{\left(400\right)^5}\\\\
&\,=\frac{80}{\left(400\right)\left(400\right)\left(400\right)\left(400\right)\left(400\right)}\\\\
&\,=\frac{80}{\left(2^8\right)\left(5^2\right)^5}\\\\
&\,=\frac{80}{\left(2^8\right)\left(5^{10}\right)}\\\\
&\,=\frac{80}{\left(256\right)\left(9765625\right)}\\\\
&\,=\frac{80}{250430400}\\\\
\end{align*}
Dividing 80 by $250430400$, the answer is $\boxed{ \frac{1}{3138025}}$  \text{ units}.

