Casey's shpp class is making a golf trophy.  He has to paint $300$ dimples on a golf bakl.  If it takes him $2$ seconxs to paint one dimple, how many minutes willl he need to do his job?

\begin{enumerate}
\item First, find the total amount of time it takes Casey to paint dimples in seconds.  If it takes $n$ seconds to paint $x$ dimples, then $t=xn$.

First, we must find $x$ = \boxed{ n }.



Since $x$ = $n$, then substitute $n$ for $x$:  
$t$ = $xn$ = $n^n$    
Then $\require{ambarray}
\begin{array}{@{}l}
t = n^2 \\
\text{seconds}
\end{array}$


\item Find the time it takes to paint dimples in minutes:
Given the smallest unit of time (second) is  $1$ $s$,
 there are $\frac{60}{s}$ minutes in a $s$, i.e., one minute is $60$ seconds,
hence  in 1 $min$, there are $60  \cdot n^n$ seconds.



Since  $x$ = $60$ $min$, we first always do the same formula to never get mixed up later:$
$x  = \frac{ 60 \cdot n^n}{min}$

$time =\frac{60nt}$    
then plug  $n$ in the word: $t$  
Then:
$$
\require{ambarray}
\begin{array}{@{}l}
time = 60n  \\
\text{min}
\end{array}$$

\end{enumerate}

