The number of ways to choose $g$ 2 girls, choose 2 girls out of 4, use the combination formula
g=\frac{n \times (n-1)}{2 \times 1} \\
\)= \frac{4 \times 3}{2 \times 1}
\\= \frac{12}{2}
\\= 6
